{"task":"SWORD II/III continuation + SWORD III correction campaign install, TUNGSTEN. Trigger phrases: 'sword master tungsten' (SWORD II loop) and SWORD_III.md is now installed alongside it at '# ETERNIUS GROUP\\tungsten\\SWORD_III.md' as an addition, not a replacement.","paused_reason":"Manuel asked to save state ('save stae all'). Deliberate clean save point, not a hang or failure. terminal.exe is manually closed (Manuel closed it himself mid-session, said 'stop watching live for now' and 'im manually closing mt4') -- no live run in progress, no monitor armed.","current_true_state":"Latest build: TUNGSTEN_10.64_A7.5_QUANT_SLS(150).mq4/.ex4, compiled 0 errors/0 warnings/643ms, deployed byte-identical (MD5 86b8d89e57aa52943c280ec94f56041b) across all 3 locations ('# EX MACHINA\\focus\\x_strategies ix\\ELITE FIXES\\', the x_strategies ix root, and the live terminal's MQL4\\Experts folder). ExportHistoricalScoreOutcomes is TRUE in source -- deliberately, so the NEXT restart (whenever authorized) automatically captures WARRANT#184's new r_continuous/mfe_atr/mae_atr columns. forge_ledger.json synced through pass_185 (both the ELITE FIXES canonical copy and the MQL4\\Files mirror).","sword_iii_installed":"SWORD_III.md (the correction campaign -- builds on SWORD_II_MASTER.md, does not replace it) installed at '# ETERNIUS GROUP\\tungsten\\SWORD_III.md', cleaned from a supplied .docx. Focus: 8 (now correctly understood as 6, W-4/5/6 merged per its own Rule III-22) named logics that work exactly as designed but destroy value by design -- blending indicators (W-1), fixed break-even (W-2), single-instrument (W-3), decide-once-never-reread (merged W-4), Kelly's flat window (W-7), miscalibrated success bar (W-8). Part I (audit the evidence before building on it) declared BLOCKING and is now substantially closed -- see warrant summary below.","warrants_this_session_176_through_184":"WARRANT#176: Strong Bear live inversion trim (prior session). WARRANT#177/179/180: historical export + regime tagging + per-regime IC/AUC, all null at real power (prior + this session). WARRANT#181: corrected a STALE capability-register entry -- R-2 (CSCV/PBO overfitting check) was live-verified working since 2026-07-19 (WARRANT#79), master doc wrongly said 'NOT BUILT'. WARRANT#182 (shipped, SLS149->150 lineage): g_RegimeIC[9][6] per-component-per-regime IC was ALREADY computed+consumed live every run but silenced from the log by g_CalibSilent -- one TLog() call fixes it, answers SWORD III Part 3.1's decision point on the next run, zero new pipeline. WARRANT#183: flipped ExportHistoricalScoreOutcomes false then true again (184 needs it). WARRANT#184 (shipped): proved magnitude-IC/W-2's 'total R' was mathematically degenerate on the old fixed-bracket export (rank-invariant to a monotonic relabeling, verified bit-for-bit identical) -- added mfe_atr/mae_atr/bars_to_mfe/bars_to_mae/r_continuous columns, real continuous R for every row including previously-censored unresolved ones.","g_self_and_purgedcv_resolved":"cerberus.py: built validate_finding() -- gate_self() existed since pass_161 but nothing ever called it (the exact 'registry not enforcement' gap). Now composes G-REACH+G-POWER+G-STALE+G-SELF into one accept/reject decision, self-tested against the F6/V-4-V-5 incident shape + a compounded-failure case. Scope stated honestly: validates a Finding OBJECT, does not migrate forge_ledger.json's prose entries to structured records (separate future work). purgedcv-0.1.4 and skfolio-1.0.0 installed AND validated (not just pip-trusted) -- CombinatorialPurgedCV produces exactly C(6,2)=15 paths in both independent libraries, deflated_sharpe_ratio correctly crushes significance 0.95->0.00 as trials go 1->100. All 5 newly-validated instruments registered in cerberus's INSTRUMENT_VALIDATION_REGISTRY. All 10 cerberus self-tests + full run_cerberus.py pipeline re-verified passing.","self_inflicted_mistake_this_session":"Mid-WARRANT#184-edit, mistakenly ran a version-bump sed directly on the already-shipped SLS(149).mq4 in ELITE FIXES (meant to copy-then-edit, edited in place instead) -- briefly corrupted its EA_VERSION/EA_BUILD_ID strings and left WARRANT#184 code under the wrong filename. Caught immediately via a version-string grep, fixed by restoring from the untouched root/Experts copies (deployed before the mistake, confirmed clean and MD5-matching each other), not by hand-patching. All 3 locations re-verified byte-identical afterward. Logged, not hidden.","live_run_state_at_pause":"No live run in progress -- terminal.exe manually closed by Manuel this session, after Phase 3B of the post-restart run completed all 9 regimes (real finding: 'MOSTLY TIME-VARYING -- majority of regimes show real, measured non-stationary structure ... a single fixed-window linear search cannot capture this by design, not evidence the signal is absent' -- logged as WARRANT#182-adjacent finding in pass_181). No live trade has ever closed in this project's history -- TUNGSTEN_pathstate_export.csv and net_b remain honestly INSUFFICIENT_DATA. Explicit instruction in effect: 'no live testing yet' -- nothing shipped this session was tested by relaunching the terminal.","next_when_resumed":"(1) When Manuel authorizes live testing again: relaunch terminal.exe from 'C:\\Program Files (x86)\\XM Global MT4\\terminal.exe', confirm USDJPY M5 + build MD5 86b8d89e57aa52943c280ec94f56041b via MQL4\\Logs\\<date>.log. (2) Watch for WARRANT#182's new 'P2-IC' TLog lines during Phase 2 -- this is the FIRST time per-component-per-regime IC will ever have been visible; run research_layer analysis against it the moment it appears, this directly answers SWORD III Part 3.1's decision point (blend cancelling real components vs components individually null). (3) Once that run also reaches Phase 0 (historical export), confirm TUNGSTEN_historical_score_export.csv now has the 5 new WARRANT#184 columns with real values, then re-run analyze_historical_scores.py/analyze_regime_breakdown.py using r_continuous instead of won for a genuine magnitude-IC test (not degenerate this time). (4) After that, flip ExportHistoricalScoreOutcomes back to false, recompile, redeploy (safe any time, editing/compiling never affects an already-running instance). (5) Continue SWORD III's Part F queue: item 1 (per-component IC) should now be answerable; items 4/5 (success-bar reset to IC 0.02-0.05, W-2 total-R recompute) can proceed once WARRANT#184's data exists. (6) Continue the standing fix->build->wait-for-consent->observe loop -- do not restart the terminal without explicit authorization, per this session's 'no live testing yet' instruction, which stands until Manuel says otherwise.","explicitly_not_done":"CEA (Part VII) not implemented in MQL4. R-2's generalization beyond Phase 3B's specific weight-search context to a general CEA-ready overfitting check (Rule I.12 scope discipline -- correctly deferred, not rushed). Full IX.3 ledger-to-structured-records migration (forge_ledger.json pass_N entries remain prose). W-3 breadth extension (6 pairs, 5 years) -- needs new symbol history or a live-attached run, execution-adjacent, held pending consent. T0-2/T0-4 (a completed calibration, a forward test) -- need real elapsed live time, not more code.","where_the_full_detail_lives":"forge_ledger.json (ELITE FIXES + MQL4\\Files, synced through pass_185) has every warrant/finding in full technical detail. '# ETERNIUS GROUP\\tungsten\\SWORD_II_STATUS.md' is the 30-second human-readable version, current through pass_184-185. '# ETERNIUS GROUP\\tungsten\\SWORD_III.md' is the installed correction-campaign charter, with Part I and Part F corrected in-place this session (not just cited, edited). research_layer\\ holds analyze_historical_scores.py, analyze_regime_breakdown.py, audit_export_evidence.py, audit_export_evidence_round2.py (all runnable, all self-tested). cerberus\\cerberus.py/run_cerberus.py hold the validation gates including the new validate_finding().","ts":"2026-08-26T19:20:00+02:00"}
